From: BOQ parser / countdown lane
Subject: [PATCH] read the Etimad quantities table from coordinates, report a
 partial read as partial, and estimate the wait from measured throughput

Applies to: 4d15d36 (farqconstraction). Verified with `git apply --binary` into
a pristine worktree at that revision: tsc clean, 235 tests pass, including the
end-to-end assertion against the booklet itself.

Independent of the SendModal narrowing patch (4d15d36, already landed) and of
the API-repository patches. Touches no file another lane holds.

CONTAINS ITS OWN UNTRACKED DEPENDENCIES
---------------------------------------
Four of the eight files are new, and the three changed files do not build
without them. They are in this patch, not after it:

  src/lib/boqPdfTable.ts        required by src/lib/parseBoq.ts
  src/lib/boqEta.ts             required by src/views/UploadView.tsx and parseBoq.ts
  src/lib/boqPdfTable.test.ts   new suite
  src/lib/boqEta.test.ts        new suite
  fixtures/boq/reference-etimad-2020-48.pdf        read by boqPdfTable.test.ts
  fixtures/boq/reference-etimad-groundtruth.json   read by boqPdfTable.test.ts

The two fixtures are the reason this patch is 7MB. They are not optional: the
end-to-end test reads the booklet itself, so applying the code without them
turns the one test that proves the claim into a failure at CI rather than a
silent pass.

  src/lib/parseBoq.ts           changed
  src/views/UploadView.tsx      changed

WHAT IT DELIVERS
----------------
1. 68 of 68 items from the canonical Etimad booklet with the booklet's own item
   number, quantity and unit. Was 0 — «لم نعثر على بنود» — because the page
   collapsed to one line per page and Arabic arrived as presentation forms.
   Read from glyph coordinates, since that table has no drawn column rules.

2. A partial read can no longer present as a complete one. The count is
   reported against the booklet's own numbering, before supplier matching, and
   names the items it could not read.

3. An expected-time-to-finish derived only from measured throughput, which says
   «لم نقِس ما يكفي بعد» rather than inventing a number, and keeps counting
   honestly when it overruns.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DELIVER
------------------------
Not the 13.9s → 2.8s latency win reported earlier. That was skipping the
server PDF parse when the column read was complete, and it is withdrawn:

  - the 10.1s it saved no longer exists. Measured again on 16 Sep against the
    local API: the same booklet parses server-side in 11ms, and the last
    serverRead sample in the browser was 16ms. The measurement the win rested
    on describes a service that has since been fixed.
  - skipping that call discarded the technical specification text. The
    quantities table prints no specification column; that text lives in a
    separate section, and only the API reads it. A specless line matches on its
    name alone, which is how ppr-pipes becomes pvc-pipe.

So the call stays, on a 6s leash when the column read is already complete, and
its specification text is attached to the column reader's rows — 66 of 68 on
the reference booklet. Cost measured in Chrome: 2.8s → 3.5s total. There is no
smaller latency-only patch to ship first; that option does not survive the
re-measurement.

MEASUREMENTS THIS PATCH REPRODUCES
----------------------------------
  68/68 correct quantity and unit      npx vitest run src/lib/boqPdfTable.test.ts
  66/68 rows carry specification text  requires a reachable API; asserted in unit
                                       form by the three withApiSpecs cases
  no fixture reads fewer lines than before HEAD (regression run over 10 PDFs,
  6 archive CSV/TXT, and the named-header xlsx path: 399 lines, byte-identical)

The two rows without specification text are #29 and #30, both named
«بردورات خرسانة» with different quantities. The merge refuses an ambiguous
name rather than guessing which specification belongs to which quantity.

NOT IN THIS PATCH, AND URGENT
-----------------------------
The owner's production upload does not run this code. farq.sa serves
~/farq/Frontend (ConstructionPage.tsx), which has its own local column reader.
Measured against the same booklet and ground truth: it reads 67 of 68 with name,
quantity, unit and item number all correct, and silently drops item #23
«طبقة عازلة للرطوبة أفقية ورأسية من البيتومين الساخن» = 110 م² — the
wrapped-cell case, quantity on the middle of three rows. It also carries no
specification text at all (0 of 67), which is why every row on his screen reads
«لا توجد مواصفات إضافية». Its local read takes 320ms, so his slowness is not
there. Details and evidence in
.handoff/BOQ_PRODUCTION_PATH_AND_SPEC_LOSS_2026_09_16.md.

